 announcements; you can override this with the role prop. AlertClose is a real button labelled \\\"Dismiss alert\\\", and returnFocusRef moves focus to an element you choose when closing hides the focused control. During the exit the alert is removed from pointer events, focus order and the accessibility tree. With reduced motion enabled, the alert and icon only fade, without sliding, scaling or layout springs.\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}],[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"How do I make a dismissible alert in React?\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"How do I make a dismissible alert in React?\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-1\",\"children\":\"Render Alert with AlertIcon, AlertContent (holding AlertTitle and AlertDescription) and AlertClose. Clicking AlertClose calls dismiss, which closes the alert and fires onOpenChange(false).\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Can I control whether the alert is visible?\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Can I control whether the alert is visible?\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-1\",\"children\":\"Yes. Pass open and onOpenChange for controlled visibility, or defaultOpen for uncontrolled use. Custom children can read and change the state through the useAlert hook, which returns open, variant, setOpen and dismiss.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"How do I add buttons or links to an alert?\",{\"children\":[\"$L44\",\"$L45\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Updated\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-10-18\",\"children\":\"Oct 18, 2026\"}]]}]\n33:[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"h-fit w-fit rounded-md bg-foreground/5 px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-foreground\",\"children\":[\"returnFocusRef\",